<title>USA: U.S. agency seeks to join UPS suit - WSJ.</title>
<headline>U.S. agency seeks to join UPS suit - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Equal Employment Opportunity Commission is seeking to join a class-action racial discrimination lawsuit against United Parcel Service of America Inc, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Monday's electronic edition, the Journal said the EEOC filed a motion in St. Louis federal court seeking to join the lawsuit, which had been filed by three African-American managers.</p>
<p>The three managers accuse the company of refusing to promote qualified blacks to executive positions with higher pay and wider responsibilities.</p>
<p>The agency's request must be approved by the presiding judge.</p>
<p>UPS has denied the allegations.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
